# GCE cost and resource audit

Invoke with `@gce-status`. **Agent runs terminal via Shell; never paste these commands for the user.**

**Goal:** Audit what is billing on `pt-vela`: VM state, machine type, accelerators, disks, GCS bucket.

**Judgment:** `.cursor/skills/gce-ops/SKILL.md`

| Name | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Project ID | `pt-vela` |
| VM | `vst-vela-01` |
| Zone | `europe-west4-a` |
| Bucket | `pt-vela-gce` |

---

## Agent workflow

From repo root on **Mac**:

```sh
gcloud config get-value project
gcloud projects list --format="table(projectId,name)"
chmod +x scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh billing-status
```

**Red flags (escalate to user):**

| Finding | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| `status: RUNNING` and user not actively working | `@gce-stop` |
| `accelerators` not `none` | Stop VM; plan GPU removal (recreate without `--accelerator`) |
| `machine_type` above `n1-standard-4` while idle | `remote.sh downsize` after stop |
| Extra VMs in project list | Report names; stop unused instances |

**Console cross-check (user):** Billing → Reports → Compute Engine → group by SKU (last 24h).

